    "justification": "Consistency and transport identify the causal contrast for the labelled point \\(\\xi_P(z_0)\\) after centering makes the treated mean common across replicas.",
    "gap": "Observed-law uniqueness of \\(m_s(z_{0s})\\) does not verify event-date transport.",
    "consumer": "Headline results first target \\(\\theta_{\\mathrm{ker}}\\) and invoke this lemma only after the labelled transfer point has been constructed.",
    "proof_tex": "For a panel law \\(P\\), Definition \\texttt{def:target} gives, at every query\nwhere the displayed conditional expectations exist,\n\\[\n \\tau(z_0)=\\sum_{s=1}^{S}\\pi_s\\left\\{\n \\mathbb E_P[B_{si}(1)\\mid z_0]-\n \\mathbb E_P[B_{si}(0)\\mid z_0]\\right\\}.                    \\tag{1}\n\\]\nAssumption \\texttt{ass:design-conditional-centering} gives a common value\n\\[\n \\mathbb E_P[B_{si}^{\\mathrm{obs}}\\mid z_0]=\\mu_s(z_0)\n \\quad\\text{for every replica \\(i\\)}                         \\tag{2}\n\\]\noutside a marginally null set.  The almost-sure equality in\n\\texttt{ass:consistency} disintegrates to\n\\[\n \\mathbb E_P[B_{si}(1)\\mid z_0]\n =\\mathbb E_P[B_{si}^{\\mathrm{obs}}\\mid z_0],                \\tag{3}\n\\]\nand \\texttt{ass:event-date-transport} gives\n\\[\n \\mathbb E_P[B_{si}(0)\\mid z_0]=m_s(z_{0s}).                 \\tag{4}\n\\]\nThere are finitely many cohorts and replicas at a fixed triangular-array\nindex.  Intersecting the conull sets for (2)--(4) and substituting into (1)\nproves the panel-law display in the lemma, including its independence of the\nreplica label.\n\nNow fix an admissible query and a labelled point\n\\(\\xi=(\\mathbb K_\\xi;\\mu,m,\\Sigma)\\in\n\\mathcal M_{N,T,\\mathbf n}(z_0)\\).  Equations (2)--(3) in\nDefinition \\texttt{def:fixed-query-kernel-class} give, for every \\(i\\),\n\\[\n \\mathbb E_{\\mathbb K_\\xi}B_{si}^{\\mathrm{obs}}=\\mu_s,\n \\qquad B_{si}^{\\mathrm{obs}}=B_{si}(1)\\ \\text{almost surely},\n \\qquad\n \\mathbb E_{\\mathbb K_\\xi}B_{si}(0)=m_s(z_{0s}).            \\tag{5}\n\\]\nBounded wealth makes all expectations finite.  Hence (5) and\nDefinition \\texttt{def:target} imply\n\\[\n \\tau(z_0)=\\sum_{s=1}^{S}\\pi_s\\{\\mu_s-m_s(z_{0s})\\}\n =\\theta_{\\mathrm{ker}}(\\xi;z_0),                            \\tag{6}\n\\]\nwhere the last equality is Definition\n\\texttt{def:fixed-query-functional}.  Thus consistency and transport prove\nthe relationship between the causal target and the observed-law functional;\nthe relationship is not imposed by definition.  No density, mixing, donor,\nrank, inversion, or division condition is used.",
